-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",29,{
[897]="70034C40\n1\tBurn Orc bodies (total: 6)\tThe western gate of Forlaw is the site of the Battle at Forlaw's Gate. Many bodies of dead Orcs can still be found there, as not many men remain in Forlaw for tasks beyond the security of the city.\n2\tCyneberg is awaiting your return in Thrymm's Home, near the southern gate of Forlaw.\t\n",
[898]="70020EFA\n1\tFind Amarion the Ranger near the Black Dens\tAmarion is in the Black Dens, south-east of Echad Dagoras. Braigiar has asked you to find Amarion and rescue him from the Shadow-wolves.\n2\tHelp Amarion escape from the Black Dens\tAmarion is at the Black Dens, south-east of Echad Dagoras. Amarion has asked for your help to escape from the Black Dens.\n3\tTalk to Amarion at Echad Dagoras\tAmarion is at Echad Dagoras, north-west of the Black Dens. You should speak with Amarion about your escape from the Shadow-wolves.\n",
[899]="70025965\n1\tCollect norbog-shells (total: 8)\tNorbog-shells can be found on the sand-nerbyg within the southern dunes of the Barandalf, north of Dwaling. Pearl Goodbody has asked you to gather shells off the nerbyg living within the dunes.\n2\tBring the norbog-shells to Pearl Goodbody in Dwaling\tPearl Goodbody is at Hob Hillbrow's just outside of Dwaling. Pearl Goodbody will want to begin extracting the green from the norbog-shells as soon as possible.\n",
[900]="7000189D\n1\tBring the aurochs skull to Ragnarr.\030Collect the aurochs skull\tThe aurochs skull can be found in the Warg territory to the north-east of the Earth-kin camp. In order to regain the trust of the Earth-kin, Ragnarr Hornsounder has asked you to collect an aurochs skull from the totem in the hills of eastern Nan Amlug and return it to him at the Earth-kin camp. A group of Wargs currently roam this territory.\n",
[901]="7002818A\n1\tCollect ledger-pages (total: 6)\tThe missing pages of the ledger have been taken by the Dragon-clan raiders in the hills to the east of the broken caravan. You should recover the missing pages of Andras' ledger.\n2\tReturn the pages to the ledger\tThe ledger is with Andras' belongings in his caravan on the northern road in Starkmoor. The pages should be placed back within the ledger.\n",
[902]="7002EEF4\n1\tFind a place to look for the eyes Béortnoth saw\tFangorn lies to the west of Thornhope. You should go near Fangorn and look for signs of the eyes that Béortnoth claims he saw.\n2\tLook for the eyes Béortnoth claims he saw\tYou should now look for the eyes that Béortnoth claims he saw.\n3\tTalk to Thane Béortnoth near Thornhope\tThane Béortnoth is camped near the ruins of Thornhope to the east. You should return to Béortnoth and assure him that the trees do not have eyes and that they are not watching.\n",
[903]="7005AFFE\n1\tCollect twistbeard (total: 10)\tTwistbeard can found on rocks in Azanulbizar. Thorin has asked you to gather twistbeard for the Dwarves of the Haban'akkâ.\n2\tDeliver the twistbeard to Thorin at Amdân\tThorin can be found at Amdân. You have collected a great deal of twistbeard and should now deliver it to Thorin.\n",
[904]="7001AAC6\n1\tTalk to Bonny Thatcher at the Three-farrow Crafting-hall\tThe Three-farrow Crafting-hall lies to the north of the Bree Town Hall, through the Trader's Gate. Graeme Tenderlarch has bid you to enter the Three-farrow Crafting-hall and speak with Bonny Thatcher.\n2\tTalk to Second-watcher Heathstraw near the Boar Fountain\tThe Boar Fountain lies a little to the north of the Three-farrow Crafting-hall. Bonny Thatcher told you to speak with Second-watcher Heathstraw at the Boar Fountain in the Market Square.\n3\tTalk to Lalia inside of Lalia's Market\tLalia's Market is just north of the Boar Fountain in the Market Square. Second-watcher Heathstraw has suggested you browse Lalia's Market and speak with the proprietor.\n4\tTalk to Barliman Butterbur at The Prancing Pony Inn\tThe Prancing Pony Inn is north of the Market Square. Lalia has instructed you to speak with Barliman Butterbur, proprietor of The Prancing Pony Inn.\n5\tTalk to Lily Sandheaver at her home\tLily Sandheaver's home is west of The Prancing Pony Inn. Barliman Butterbur told you to speak with Lily Sandheaver at her home.\n6\tTalk to Harry Goatleaf at the West-gate\tHarry Goatleaf can be found at the West-gate, west of Lily Sandheaver's home. Lily Sandheaver told you to speak with Harry Goatleaf.\n7\tTalk to Watchman Cardoon in Bree\tWatchman Cardoon is east of the West-gate of Bree. Harry Goatleaf told you to speak with Watchman Cardoon.\n8\tTalk to Tad Gardener at the vault\030Talk to Maud Foxglove at the vault\tThe vault is found to the south of Watcher Cardoon. He told you to follow the road and look for the large, stone building protected by two guards. Watcher Cardoon instructed you to speak with Tad Gardener or Maud Foxglove at the vault.\n9\tTalk to Clar Whitethorn at Whitethorn's Taxidermy\tYou will find Whitethorn's Taxidermy across the road from the Bree-town Vault. You were told to speak with Clar Whitethorn at Whitethorn's Taxidermy.\n10\tTalk to Newbold Leafcutter\tMake your way south out of Whitethorn's Taxidery before you reach the statue of the dwarf turn left, to the east, and make your way to Scholar's Stair. Enter and speak with Newbold Leafcutter. Clar Whitethorn directed you to speak with Newbold Leafcutter within the Scholar's Stair.\n11\tTalk to Mat Heathertoes in Beggar's Alley\tMat Heathertoes is found in Beggar's Alley, south-west from Scholar's Stair, then west under the Mud Gate from the Stone Quarter. Newbold Leafcutter told you to speak with Mat Heathertoes next.\n12\tTalk to Lily Appledore at the Bree Jail\tThe Bree Jail can be found by following the road east through Bree past the Bree Town Hall, then bearing south. Mat Heathertoes suggested you speak with Lily Appledore at the Bree Jail.\n13\tThe Bree Auction Hall lies east through the Woodsmen's Gate, then south. Dawn Appledore instructed you to speak with one of the auctioneers at the Auction Hall.\t\n14\tTalk to Tad Leafcutter at the hunting-lodge\tTad Leafcutter is outside the hunting lodge, which can be found by following the road outside of the Bree Auction Hall west to its end. You have been instructed to speak with Tad Leafcutter.\n15\tTalk to Mayor Graeme Tenderlarch at the Bree Town Hall\tGraeme Tenderlarch is at the Bree Town Hall, almost due north-west from the South-gate. Tad Leafcutter told you to return to Graeme Tenderlarch.\n",
[905]="7002B8B8\n1\tSpeak to Mayor Whitfoot at the Farmers Faire\tMayor Whitfoot can be found in the centre of Bywater during the Farmers Faire festival. You should speak with Mayor Whitfoot.\n2\tSpeak with Godo Bracegirdle at the Pond in Bywater\tFishing in the Shire is most often found at the Fishing Hole just to the north of Bywater. You should head up to the pond to see if fishing is part of the Farmers Faire.\n3\tSpeak with Caltha Tunnelly, the Festival Announcer, about the Egg Scramble event\tThe Festival Announcer, Caltha Tunnelly, should know of a shortcut to Sandson's Farm. You should speak with Caltha Tunnelly once again.\n4\tTravel to Sandson's Farm to see the Egg Scramble event\tWymarc Grubb is at Sandson's Farm in the Shire, just east of Michel and Little Delving. You should speak with Wymarc Grubb about the Egg Scramble event.\n5\tTravel to Bamfurlong to see the delicious, tempting mushrooms\tBamfurlong, Farmer Maggot's renowned farm, is in the Marish in the south-eastern corner of the Shire. The Mushroom-thieving takes place there. The farm can be reached by using the horse at Bywater. You should speak with Osbert Puddifoot at Bamfurlong.\n6\tSpeak with the Festival Announcer, Caltha Tunnelly, in Bywater\tCaltha Tunnelly, the Festival Announcer, is at the Farmers Faire in Bywater. You should speak with Caltha Tunnelly to finish the tour of the Farmers Faire.\n",
[906]="70065DD3\n1\tSearch the waggon\tYou found an abandoned waggon with phials of a familiar substance. This could be the mode of transport Indagir used. You should search the waggon to support your theory.\n2\tFollow the trail of spills into Tumladen\tThis seems like the same substance you encountered in Thaurisgar. There is a trail of broken phials. You should follow the trail leading into Tumladen.\n3\tFollow the trail of spills into Tumladen\tThe bile spills seem to follow the road into Tumladen.\n4\tFollow the trail of spills into Tumladen\tThe bile spills seem to follow the road into Tumladen.\n5\tFollow the trail further into town\tThe bile spills have led to Tumladen and keep going further into town.\n6\tFollow the trail up the road\tThe trail is getting shorter and shorter and must end soon.\n7\tThe trail has led to a dead end\tThe trail seems to have led to a dead end.\n8\tTalk to waggon driver\tThe trail of spilled substance has led you to an injured waggon driver.\n",
[907]="70045105\n1\tSearch for a trail\tLook for a trail in the Mouths of Entwash that might lead you to Malhar.\n2\tFollow the trail\tFollow the trail in the Mouths of Entwash that might lead you to Malhar.\n3\tFollow the trail\tFollow the trail in the Mouths of Entwash that might lead you to Malhar.\n4\tFollow the trail\tFollow the trail in the Mouths of Entwash that might lead you to Malhar.\n5\tFollow the trail\tFollow the trail in the Mouths of Entwash that might lead you to Malhar.\n6\tGo up the hill\tThe last clue in the trail points up a hill, deep in the Mouths of Entwash. You should see what is there.\n7\tTalk to the young man\tTalk to the young man in the clearing on the hill in the Mouths of Entwash.\n",
[908]="70035B0D\n1\tSolve the mystery of the slain Orcs\tCyneberg is in the northern High Knolls, kneeling over a pile of slain Orcs. You should speak with Cyneberg.\n2\tSpeak with Gárwig\tGárwig is in the Mead Hall of Forlaw. You should speak with Gárwig.\n",
[909]="7003707A\n1\tBring the brigands' note to Thane Ordlac\tThane Ordlac is in the Mead Hall of Oserley. Dudsig asked you to bring the note you found to Thane Ordlac.\n",
[910]="7006A761\n1\tSearch for Tirneldir at the fish traps outside the southern gate\tArthiel has not seen Tirneldir for some time and told you he may be at his fish traps to the south of Lond Cirion.\n2\tCheck the area for signs of Tirneldir\tThere was no sign of Tirneldir at the fish traps just outside of the southern gate in Lond Cirion, he may be at other traps nearby.\n3\tSpeak with Tirneldir\tYou have found Tirneldir outside of the southern gate in Lond Cirion. You should speak with him as he appears injured and scared.\n4\tReturn to Lindil\tTirneldir has asked you to return to Lindil back near the northern gate in upper Lond Cirion.\n",
[911]="7005479E\n1\tSet traps in the encampment of Urshúlagar (total: 4)\030Set traps in Urshúlagar\030Set traps in the encampment of Angathrai (total: 4)\030Set traps in Angathrai\030Set traps in the encampment of Matum Graz (total: 4)\030Set traps in Matum Graz\tEnemy encampments can be found throughout Emyn Duir. You should hide traps at these encampments to confuse the enemy forces within.\n2\tCompleted\tSet many traps in encampments throughout Emyn Duir.\n",
[912]="7000B958\n1\tTalk to Garbert and carry out his plan to capture the creature\tGarbert is at his cottage south of Echad Candelleth, at a fork in the river Bruinen. You should speak with Garbert when you are ready to carry out his plan to capture the creature.\n2\tTalk to Garbert\tGarbert is at his cottage south of Echad Candelleth, at a fork in the river Bruinen. You should speak with Garbert regarding the creature.\n3\tBring the arrows to Wistan\tWistan is at his camp-fire at Echad Candelleth, the Elf-camp in Tâl Bruinen, north of Garbert's cottage. Garbert suggested that you bring Wistan's arrows back to him.\n",
[913]="7003302F\n1\tMine mineral deposits (total: 8)\tOre can be found in the mineral deposits and on the deep-claws that line the crevasse in southern Zelem-melek. You should gather ore from this mineral-rich area.\n2\tSearch deep-claws for minerals (total: 4)\tOre can be found in the mineral deposits and on the deep-claws that line the crevasse in southern Zelem-melek. You should gather ore from this mineral-rich area.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have harvested many rare minerals from the treacherous crevasse in southern Zelem-melek.\n",
[914]="7002C005\n1\tTalk to Gnarlstump\tGnarlstump can be found near the desolation of the Entwives' gardens in the Brown Lands. You should bring the flower to Gnarlstump at once.\n",
[915]="70071DFA\n1\tRecover \"The Farings of Kábuzar Volume I\"\030Defeat Ordâkhai within the Halls of Lajór (total: 12)\tRecover the first volume of the book \"The Farings of Kábuzar\" from inside the Halls of Lajór in Zajâna.\n2\tRecover \"The Farings of Kábuzar Volume II\"\tRecover the second volume of the book \"The Farings of Kábuzar\" from inside the Halls of Lajór in Zajâna.\n3\tEscape with the books before more Ordâkhai arrive!\tEscape with the books before the alarm sounds and more Ordâkhai arrive! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[916]="7003EA7D\n1\tSearch for Quickbeam's Huorn\tOne of Quickbeam's Huorns can be found to the north of Derndingle. Quickbeam has asked you to seek out one of his Huorns in Fangorn Forest as he hopes to ask for their aid.\n2\tSearch for Quickbeam's Huorn\tAnother of Quickbeam's Huorns can be found to the west of Derndingle. Quickbeam has asked you to seek out one of his Huorns in Fangorn Forest. After finding the first Huorn turned tree-ish, you should continue your search.\n3\tSearch for Quickbeam's Huorn\tQuickbeam's Huorn can be found to the south-west of Derndingle in Fangorn Forest. You have discovered two of Quickbeam's Huorns, but they were slain or tree-ish. You should search for Quickbeam's Huorn in the last location he mentioned.\n4\tPoke at Quickbeam's Huorn\tQuickbeam's Huorn can be found to the south-west of Derndingle. You have found a Huorn that appears to be sleeping, but still aware. You should poke it and see if it responds.\n5\tTalk to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam can be found at Derndingle in south-eastern Fangorn Forest. You have found one of Quickbeam's Huorns, and it seemed eager to return to his side. You should speak with Quickbeam.\n",
[917]="700331C7\n1\tFind the source of the tremor\tThe source of the tremor can be found in Khadar-zarâm's goblin camp atop the stair.\n2\tFind the source of the tremor\tThe source of the tremor can be found in Khadar-zarâm's goblin camp atop the stair.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated the menace upon the stair.\n",
[918]="700330D6\n1\tUse the summoning horn to call Svanr\tThe summoning horn can be found near Svanr on the stairs of Khadar-zarâm. You should summon Svanr to let him know when you are ready to depart.\n2\tLight braziers at the feet of the stone dwarves (total: 6)\tBraziers can be found at the feet of the dwarf-statues along the north edge of Nud-melek's Second Hall. You should light the braziers as a tribute to the fine stone-work of Durin's day.\n3\tTalk to Svanr (use the horn to summon him)\tSvanr can be summoned using the horn. You should speak with Svanr.\n4\tFind the Bridge of Khazad-dûm with Svanr\tThe Bridge of Khazad-dûm is east of the stone dwarves in the Second Hall. You should travel with Svanr to the Bridge of Khazad-dûm.\n5\tTalk to Svanr (use the horn to summon him)\tThe Bridge of Khazad-dûm is east of the stone dwarves in the Second Hall. You should travel with Svanr to the Bridge of Khazad-dûm.\n6\tTalk to Svanr upon the Bridge of Khazad-dûm\tSvanr is at the Bridge of Khazad-dûm.\n",
[919]="700688AC\n1\tExamine the broken crate\tThe broken crate can be found near Tâbrim on the piers of the Sail-haven. Tâbrim has asked you to examine the broken crate. You should inspect the broken crate.\n2\tFollow the trail of damaged stonework and find the escaped creature\tThe escaped creature can be found somewhere in the Sail-haven. Tâbrim informed you that the creature tore up some stonework as it fled into the Sail-haven. You should follow the damaged stonework and see where it leads.\n3\tCarefully approach the cave-claw\tThe cave-claw can be found in a small alley in the Sail-haven. You have found a fearful cave-claw, and it is clearly overwhelmed by its new home. You should carefully approach the cave-claw.\n4\tCollect a potato from one of the nearby sacks\tSacks of potatoes can be found in a small alley in the Sail-haven. You have found the cave-claw, but it appears very uneasy. You should find something you can offer it to help calm it down.\n5\tKindly offer the potato to the cave-claw\tThe cave-claw can be found in a small alley in the Sail-haven. You have collected a fine potato, and you should offer it to the frightened cave-claw.\n6\tTalk to Henok\tHenok can be found in a small alley in the Sail-haven. One of the Temámir, Henok, has arrived to collect his companion. You should talk to Henok.\n",
[920]="7002D0A4\n1\tTalk to Brifard\tBrifard is stationed at a camp in northern Parth Celebrant near south-east Thinglad. Stanric has asked you to attend to one of his men, Brifard.\n",
[921]="70046C4D\n1\tListen to Anborn's tale\tAnborn can be found within Henneth Annûn in North Ithilien. Anborn has offered to tell you more of the strange Halflings and their time among the Rangers.\n2\tTalk to Anborn\tAnborn can be found within Henneth Annûn in North Ithilien. Anborn has finished his tale, and you should now ask him if there remains any more to tell.\n",
[922]="7005AB1A\n1\tHead south along the Father's Path\tThe time has come to travel high into the Welkin-lofts seeking Ausma's apprentices. You should head south with Hórin and travel along the Father's Path.\n2\tCall Hórin and talk to him\tThe bridge along the Father's Path is out. You will need to find a way around. You should talk to Hórin. Use the summoning horn to call Hórin to your side.\n3\tFind Molkha\tMolkha should be somewhere near the frozen lake south-west of Fellgát. You should find Molkha with Hórin.\n4\tTalk to Molkha in the valley\tYou have found Molkha on the frozen lake south-west of Fellgát. You should talk to Molkha to receive her report.\n5\tTalk to Molkha and hear her troubling report\tSpeak to Molkha on the frozen lake south-west of Fellgát to hear her scouting report. You should complete 'Instance: A Troubling Report.'\n6\tTalk to Molkha in the valley\tMolkha should be somewhere near the frozen lake, south-west of Fellgát. You should talk to Molkha.\n7\tTalk to Hórin in the valley\tNow that you have Molkha's report, it is time to move further up the mountain. You should talk to Hórin and decide how to proceed.\n",
[923]="7000925E\n1\tTalk to Holly Hornblower\tHolly Hornblower is north of the main square of Hobbiton. Holly has decided to give you one of her pie recipes and is waiting to speak with you.\n",
[924]="7000B2B9\n1\tTalk to Holly Hornblower\tHolly Hornblower is north of the main square of Hobbiton. Holly has decided to give you one of her pie recipes and is waiting to speak with you.\n",
[925]="70009260\n1\tTalk to Postmaster Proudfoot\tPostmaster Proudfoot is in Michel Delving, near the Town Hole. Postmaster Proudfoot has asked you to speak with him about something.\n",
[926]="700718A1\n1\tGather \"safe\" mushrooms (total: 5)\030Obtain mildly blighted crocodile meat (total: 7)\tBíralad wants to treat the scouts of Sâr Marsag to a new meal and has asked you to gather crocodile meat and mushrooms from the Lair of the Shadlúgai to the north-east.\n2\tReturn to Bíralad in Sâr Marsag\tYou have gathered mushrooms and crocodile meat that Bíralad needed for his recipe from the Lair of the Shadlúgai. Return to him in Sâr Marsag.\n",
[927]="70068BB0\n1\tCollect shipboard treasures from Kenza's ship in the Fleet-fast (total: 3)\tThe ship docked to the east holds Kenza's valuables, but it also holds deadly mutineers.\n2\tBring her valuables to Kenza in the Fleet-fast\tKenza is by the steps leading to the upper level in the Fleet-fast.\n",
[928]="7002B5B7\n1\tItems from the vendor list can be found throughout Bywater during the Farmers Faire. The vendor list is in your inventory. You should collect the items on the vendor list...but avoid collecting items that are not listed! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\t\n2\tBring the goods to Daisy Sandyman\tDaisy Sandyman is at the market stall at the Farmers Faire. You should return to Daisy Sandyman with the goods you collected.\n",
})
